  known 2022-07-14
  enters 2022-07-29
  note "MTG-1 v1, in force 2022-07-29 – 2023-12-31, published 2022-07-14; governs instalments falling due 2022-08-01 – 2023-12-31."
,11:MTG-2.tally,862:part mtg_2
  tally 2
  law
  note "MTG-2 · Overpayment. A borrower may pay off a mortgage in part or in full at any time (.1). After 36 months from disbursement no fee; before, the agreement's fee, at most 3 % of the amount and never more than a year's interest on it at the day's rate (.2)."

source mtg_2 "Mortgage Credit Act, MTG-2 Overpayment (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input mtg2_fee_cap: num question "What is the cap on an overpayment fee (MTG-2 .2)?"

input mtg2_free_months: int question "After how many months from disbursement is no overpayment fee allowed (MTG-2 .2)?"

version mtg2_v1
  cite mtg_2
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "MTG-2 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs overpayments from 2018-01-01."
  mtg2_fee_cap = 0.03 "MTG-2 v1 .2"
  mtg2_free_months = 36 "MTG-2 v1 .2"
,12:PIT-10.tally,1537:part pit_10
  tally 2
  law
  note "PIT-10 · Business income. One form a year: (a) the scale on profit, (b) 19 % of profit, (c) a flat rate on revenue (.1); elected by notice, holding until a new one (.2). Under (a) and (b) profit is revenue less costs less the social contributions paid in the period (.3). Under (c) a month's base is its revenue less the social contributions paid in it, the rest carried within the year; IT services 12 %, other services 8.5 %, a business asset's sale 10 %; base and tax rounded (.4). Advances by the 20th of the next month (.5); a separate return for (b) and (c) by 30 April (.6)."

source pit_10 "Personal Income Tax Act, PIT-10 Business income (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

index pit10_form = [scale, profit, flat]

index pit10_supply = [it, services, asset_sale]

input pit10_flat_rate[s in pit10_supply]: num question "What is the flat rate on this kind of revenue (PIT-10 .4)?"

input pit10_profit_rate: num question "What is the rate of form (b) on profit (PIT-10 .1)?"

version pit10_v1
  cite pit_10
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "PIT-10 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs tax years from 2018 and advances for months from January 2018."
  pit10_flat_rate[it] = 0.12 "PIT-10 v1 .4: IT services 12 %"
  pit10_flat_rate[services] = 0.085 "PIT-10 v1 .4: other services 8.5 %"
  pit10_flat_rate[asset_sale] = 0.10 "PIT-10 v1 .4: the sale of a business asset 10 %"
  pit10_profit_rate = 0.19 "PIT-10 v1 .1 (b): 19 % of profit"
,12:PIT-11.tally,1061:part pit_11
  tally 2
  law
  note "PIT-11 · Cars in a business. Under (a) and (b), a car used privately too counts 75 % of its running costs (.1); depreciation 20 % a year of the initial value (net price plus the VAT not deducted), 1/12 a month from the month after its entry in the asset register to the month of its sale, each month rounded to the ort half up (.2); its sale under (a) or (b) (.3); under (c) the net price is revenue at the asset-sale rate (.4)."

source pit_11 "Personal Income Tax Act, PIT-11 Cars in a business (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input pit11_depreciation: num question "What is a car's yearly depreciation rate (PIT-11 .2)?"

input pit11_running_share: num question "What share of a mixed-use car's running costs counts as costs (PIT-11 .1)?"

version pit11_v1
  cite pit_11
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "PIT-11 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs tax years from 2018."
  pit11_depreciation = 0.20 "PIT-11 v1 .2"
  pit11_running_share = 0.75 "PIT-11 v1 .1"
,12:PIT-12.tally,1452:part pit_12
  tally 2
  law
  note "PIT-12 · The sale of a dwelling. Income is the price less the sale's costs less the acquisition cost (price, transfer tax, notary) (.1); taxed only when sold before the end of the 5th year after the acquisition's year (.2); 19 % of the income less the exempt part, base and tax rounded, in the return for the sale's year (.3); the exempt part is the income times the part of the price spent on the seller's own housing within 3 years after the end of the sale's year, over the price (.4); money spent after the return is filed corrects it (.5)."

source pit_12 "Personal Income Tax Act, PIT-12 The sale of a dwelling (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input pit12_rate: num question "What is the rate on a dwelling's sale (PIT-12 .3)?"

input pit12_spend_years: int question "Within how many years after the end of the sale's year does spending on housing count (PIT-12 .4)?"

input pit12_taxed_years: int question "Until the end of which year after acquisition is a sale taxed (PIT-12 .2)?"

version pit12_v1
  cite pit_12
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "PIT-12 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs sales from 2018-01-01."
  pit12_rate = 0.19 "PIT-12 v1 .3"
  pit12_spend_years = 3 "PIT-12 v1 .4: within 3 years after the end of the year of the sale"
  pit12_taxed_years = 5 "PIT-12 v1 .2: before the end of the 5th year after the year of acquisition"
,12:PIT-13.tally,1228:part pit_13
  tally 2
  law
  note "PIT-13 · Rent let outside a business: a flat rate on the rent received in the tax year, 8.5 % up to 100 000.00 DUK and 12.5 % above, per person (.1); each co-owner on the rent times their share (.2); an advance by the 20th of the next month, the tax on the year's rent to date less the advances paid, rounded, no costs deducted (.3); settled in the return by 30 April (.4)."
  note "pit13_rate holds the rates by the person's rent of the year, read by marginal(pit13_rate, rent) (L §5.8)."

source pit_13 "Personal Income Tax Act, PIT-13 Rent (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input pit13_adv_day: int question "By what day of the next month is a rent advance paid (PIT-13 .3)?"

band pit13_rate(x: num DUK): num
  note "the flat rates on rent received (PIT-13 .1), by the year's rent to date"

