  note "PIT-3 v3, in force 2022-07-01 until replaced, published 2022-06-14; governs the tax for tax years from 2022, the whole of 2022 included, and advances paid from 2022-07-01. This version holds its rows for 2022, where they replace v2's; pit3_v3_on holds the same rows from 2023 (one act, two versions: a band table's replace rows with no earlier table on part of their span are refused by the reference interpreter, W-A fault F6)."
  replace pit3_rate: [0, 120000] = 0.13 "PIT-3 v3 .1: 13 % of the base up to 120 000.00 DUK"
  replace pit3_rate: (120000, inf) = 0.33 "PIT-3 v3 .1: 33 % of the part above 120 000.00 DUK"
  replace pit3_reducing = 3900.00 "PIT-3 v3 .2"

version pit3_v3_on
  cite pit_3
  governs 2023-01-01..
  known 2022-06-14
  enters 2022-07-01
  note "PIT-3 v3 from tax year 2023 on (see pit3_v3)."
  pit3_rate: [0, 120000] = 0.13 "PIT-3 v3 .1: 13 % of the base up to 120 000.00 DUK"
  pit3_rate: (120000, inf) = 0.33 "PIT-3 v3 .1: 33 % of the part above 120 000.00 DUK"
  pit3_reducing = 3900.00 "PIT-3 v3 .2"
,11:PIT-4.tally,1668:part pit_4
  tally 2
  law
  note "PIT-4 · Advances on employment income. The month's base is the payer's PIT-2 base rounded (.1); the advance is the scale on the year-to-date bases less the scale on the earlier ones, less 1/12 of the reducing amount where a reducing statement is on file, (v1: less the health contribution up to 7.75 % of its base), never below 0, rounded (.2). The PIT-3 wording is the one in force on the payment day."
  note "pit4_v2_p4 governs payments made 2022-07-01 – 2022-12-31: the advance is computed with PIT-3 v2 (wording of pit4_lower_wording) and with PIT-3 v3, and the lower is withheld (.4)."

source pit_4 "Personal Income Tax Act, PIT-4 Advances on employment income (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input pit4_lower_wording: date question "Which day's wording of PIT-3 is the PIT-3 v2 of PIT-4 v2 .4?"

