,11:TSB-3.tally,749:part tsb_3
  tally 2
  law
  note "TSB-3 · The bond's value: at each interest year's end the old value times one plus the year's rate, to whole orts half up, per bond (.1); inside an interest year the value at its start times one plus the rate times the days elapsed over the interest year's days, to whole orts half up, per bond (.2)."
  note "No figure: round(x, 0.01, half-up) is stated, and the day count is days(a, b) (L §4.2)."

source tsb_3 "Treasury Savings Bonds, terms of issue, TSB-3 The bond's value (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version tsb3_v1
  cite tsb_3
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-11-20
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "TSB-3 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-11-20; governs series issued from January 2018."
,11:TSB-4.tally,891:part tsb_4
  tally 2
  law
  note "TSB-4 · Early redemption: any number of bonds of a series, paid on the third business day after the request (.1); each bond its value on the request day (TSB-3.2) less a fee of 2.00 DUK, never more than the value less 100.00 (.2); at maturity the value with no fee (.3)."

source tsb_4 "Treasury Savings Bonds, terms of issue, TSB-4 Redemption before maturity (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input tsb4_days: int question "On which business day after the request is a redemption paid (TSB-4 .1)?"

input tsb4_fee: money DUK question "What is the early-redemption fee per bond (TSB-4 .2)?"

version tsb4_v1
  cite tsb_4
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-11-20
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "TSB-4 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-11-20; governs series issued from January 2018."
  tsb4_days = 3 "TSB-4 v1 .1"
  tsb4_fee = 2.00 "TSB-4 v1 .2"
,11:TSB-5.tally,653:part tsb_5
  tally 2
  law
  note "TSB-5 · Tax on the interest: on each redemption (of a series, TSB-4.1) 19 % of the amount paid per bond less 100.00 DUK, times the bonds redeemed, rounded (GEN-5.1) (.1)."

source tsb_5 "Treasury Savings Bonds, terms of issue, TSB-5 Tax on the interest (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input tsb5_rate: num question "What share of the interest is withheld on a redemption (TSB-5 .1)?"

version tsb5_v1
  cite tsb_5
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-11-20
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "TSB-5 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-11-20; governs redemptions from 2018-01-01."
  tsb5_rate = 0.19 "TSB-5 v1 .1"
,11:TSB-6.tally,627:part tsb_6
  tally 2
  law
  note "TSB-6 · Inherited bonds: they pass with their series' terms (.1); for an heir, TSB-4.2 and TSB-5 read the bond's value on the day of the death in place of 100.00 DUK (.2); divided only in whole bonds (.3)."
  note "No figure: the households' defs read the death-day value through TSB-3."

source tsb_6 "Treasury Savings Bonds, terms of issue, TSB-6 Inherited bonds (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version tsb6_v1
  cite tsb_6
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-11-20
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "TSB-6 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-11-20; governs deaths from 2018-01-01."
,11:TSB-7.tally,629:part tsb_7
  tally 2
  law
  note "TSB-7 · Bonds of spouses: bonds registered to one spouse but held in community are, at that spouse's death, half the survivor's and half in the estate (.1); the heir who takes them in the division holds all of them as an heir, TSB-6.2 applying to each, the survivor's half included (.2)."

source tsb_7 "Treasury Savings Bonds, terms of issue, TSB-7 Bonds of spouses (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version tsb7_v1
  cite tsb_7
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-11-20
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "TSB-7 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-11-20; governs deaths from 2018-01-01."
,11:TSB-8.tally,643:part tsb_8
  tally 2
  law
  note "TSB-8 · The tax withheld is final: TSB-5's withholding ends the tax on the interest, which is not stated in the holder's return (.1)."

source tsb_8 "Treasury Savings Bonds, terms of issue, TSB-8 The tax withheld is final (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input tsb8_final: bool question "Does the tax withheld on a redemption end the tax on the bond's interest (TSB-8 .1)?"

version tsb8_v1
  cite tsb_8
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-11-20
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "TSB-8 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-11-20; governs redemptions from 2018-01-01."
  tsb8_final = true "TSB-8 v1 .1"
,10:TT-1.tally,708:part tt_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "TT-1 · Transfer tax on a dwelling. The buyer from a seller who is not a VAT taxpayer pays 2 % of the market value (the price, unless below it) (.1); co-buyers each on their share of the value (.2); the notary collects it on the deed's day, rounded (.3, GEN-5 .1)."

source tt_1 "Transfer Tax Act, TT-1 Transfer tax on a dwelling (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input tt1_rate: num question "What is the transfer tax rate on a dwelling (TT-1 .1)?"

version tt1_v1
  cite tt_1
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "TT-1 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs purchases from 2018-01-01."
  tt1_rate = 0.02 "TT-1 v1 .1"
,10:TT-2.tally,884:part tt_2
  tally 2
  law
  note "TT-2 · The first-home exemption. A buyer's share is exempt where the buyer owned no dwelling and no share on the purchase day and at any time in the 5 years before (.1); an inherited share of 50 % or less doesn't count (.2); each co-buyer judged alone (.3)."
  note "Governs purchases from 2023-01-01 only: a purchase before has no candidate row, so the exemption is never read for it (L §4.6)."

source tt_2 "Transfer Tax Act, TT-2 The first-home exemption (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input tt2_lookback_years: int question "How many years before the purchase must the buyer have owned no dwelling (TT-2 .1)?"

version tt2_v1
  cite tt_2
  governs 2023-01-01..
  known 2022-09-29
  enters 2023-01-01
  note "TT-2 v1, in force 2023-01-01 until replaced, published 2022-09-29; governs purchases from 2023-01-01."
  tt2_lookback_years = 5 "TT-2 v1 .1"
,11:VAT-1.tally,585:part vat_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "VAT-1 · Taxable supplies and the rate: 22 % of the net price on supplies by a taxpayer in Lenia (.1); letting a dwelling for living in is exempt (.2)."

source vat_1 "Value Added Tax Act, VAT-1 Taxable supplies and the rate (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input vat_rate: num question "What is the VAT rate (VAT-1 .1)?"

version vat1_v1
  cite vat_1
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "VAT-1 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs supplies from 2018-01-01."
  vat_rate = 0.22 "VAT-1 v1 .1"
,11:VAT-2.tally,928:part vat_2
  tally 2
  law
  note "VAT-2 · The small-business exemption. Supplies of the previous year not above 200 000.00 DUK: exempt until the supply with which the year's supplies first go above 200 000.00 DUK, that supply included (.1); a business starting in the year has the limit times its days of activity over the year's days, rounded to the ort (.2, GEN-5 .3); exempt supplies and sales of business assets not counted (.3); the exemption may be given up from a month's first day (.4)."

source vat_2 "Value Added Tax Act, VAT-2 The small-business exemption (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input vat2_limit: money DUK question "What is the yearly small-business limit (VAT-2 .1)?"

version vat2_v1
  cite vat_2
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "VAT-2 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs supplies from 2018-01-01."
  vat2_limit = 200000.00 "VAT-2 v1 .1"
,11:VAT-3.tally,722:part vat_3
  tally 2
  law
  note "VAT-3 · The tax point and the invoice. VAT is due on the invoice's issue day; the invoice is issued by the 15th of the month after the supply (.1); the VAT is the net times the rate, rounded (.2, GEN-5 .2); on an invoice in florens the VAT is also stated in dukats, converted under GEN-4 with the issue day as the event (.3)."
  note "No figure: the households' invoice defs apply it."

source vat_3 "Value Added Tax Act, VAT-3 The tax point and the invoice (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version vat3_v1
  cite vat_3
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "VAT-3 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs supplies from 2018-01-01."
,11:VAT-4.tally,786:part vat_4
  tally 2
  law
  note "VAT-4 · The monthly return, by the 25th of the next month: the VAT on the month's invoices issued, less the input VAT deducted in the month, less the excess carried from the month before (.1); a positive result paid by the same day, a negative one carried into the next month or refunded on request within 60 days (.2); amounts rounded (.3, GEN-5 .2)."
  note "No figure: the 25th is a literal the literal rule allows (L §7.1). The households' defs apply it."

source vat_4 "Value Added Tax Act, VAT-4 The monthly return (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version vat4_v1
  cite vat_4
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "VAT-4 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs months from January 2018."
,11:VAT-5.tally,879:part vat_5
  tally 2
  law
  note "VAT-5 · Input VAT. Deducted in the month its invoice is received, or in either of the two months after (.1). A car used privately too: 50 % of the VAT on its purchase, fuel, repairs and leasing; 100 % only with business use alone and a mileage log (.2)."

source vat_5 "Value Added Tax Act, VAT-5 Input VAT (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input vat5_car_share: num question "What share of a mixed-use car's VAT is deducted (VAT-5 .2)?"

input vat5_late_months: int question "In how many months after receipt may input VAT still be deducted (VAT-5 .1)?"

version vat5_v1
  cite vat_5
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "VAT-5 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs purchase invoices received from 2018-01-01."
  vat5_car_share = 0.50 "VAT-5 v1 .2"
  vat5_late_months = 2 "VAT-5 v1 .1"
,11:VAT-6.tally,493:part vat_6
  tally 2
  law
  note "VAT-6 · Selling a business asset: VAT at 22 % of the price, whatever share of the purchase VAT was deducted (.1)."
  note "No figure: the rate is vat_rate (VAT-1)."

source vat_6 "Value Added Tax Act, VAT-6 Selling a business asset (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version vat6_v1
  cite vat_6
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "VAT-6 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs sales from 2018-01-01."
,11:WCP-1.tally,1225:part wcp_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "WCP-1 · Workplace plan contributions: the employee's basic 2 % of gross pay and up to 2 % more if declared (.2); the employer's basic 1.5 %, and up to 2.5 % more by its plan (.3); parental pay bears none; each contribution rounded to the ort (.4, GEN-5 .3); paid to the plan by the 15th of the next month; units bought at the price of the day the money is credited (.4)."

source wcp_1 "Workplace Capital Plans Act, WCP-1 Contributions (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input wcp1_ee_basic: num question "What is the employee's basic contribution (WCP-1 .2)?"

input wcp1_ee_extra_max: num question "Up to what additional contribution may the employee declare (WCP-1 .2)?"

