  cite civ_5
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-03-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "CIV-5 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-03-01; governs divisions from 2018-01-01."
,11:FAM-1.tally,2912:part fam_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "FAM-1 · The child benefit: a monthly amount for a child under 18 (.1), granted for benefit periods 1 June – 31 May; a claim filed by 30 April before the period gives it from June, a later claim from the month filed (.2; the filing day is a month-day row); for a child born during a period, a claim within 3 months of the birth gives it from the birth month, a later one from the month filed (.3); the birth month is prorated by days, rounded down to the ort (.4)."
  note "fam1_filed: the act doesn't say whether a claim sent by registered post is filed when posted or when the FBO receives it."

source fam_1 "Family Benefits Act, FAM-1 The child benefit (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

axis fam1_filed
  posted "a claim sent by registered post is filed on the day it is posted"
  received "a claim is filed on the day the FBO receives it"

index benefit_period = year 2018..2030 from 06-01
  v fam1_v1
  note "benefit periods run 1 June – 31 May (FAM-1 .2); key 2022 is 2022-06-01 – 2023-05-31"

input fam1_age: int question "Under what age is a child entitled (FAM-1 .1)?"

input fam1_amount: money DUK question "What is the monthly child benefit (FAM-1 .1)?"

input fam1_birth_months: int question "Within how many months of the birth must the claim be filed (FAM-1 .3)?"

input fam1_file_day: monthday question "On which day of the year is the last day to file a claim before its period (FAM-1 .2)?"

def fam1_file_by[p in benefit_period]: date at start_of(p)
  note "FAM-1 .2: the last day to file a claim for period p so that it gives the benefit from the period's start: the last 30 April before the period. The day is the month-day row fam1_file_day, found in the calendar year the period starts in, or the year before when that day isn't before the period's start"
  rule base = if fam1_file_in_year[p] < start_of(p) then fam1_file_in_year[p] else add_years(fam1_file_in_year[p], -1)

def fam1_file_in_year[p in benefit_period]: date at start_of(p)
  note "the filing day's month-day (fam1_file_day) in the calendar year in which period p starts"
  rule base = day_of(year_of(start_of(p)), fam1_file_day)

version fam1_v1
  cite fam_1
  governs 2018-01..2023-12
  known 2017-09-01
  note "FAM-1 v1, in force 2018-01-01 – 2023-12-31, published 2017-09-01; governs months 2018-01 – 2023-12."
  fam1_age = 18 "FAM-1 v1 .1"
  fam1_amount = 400.00 "FAM-1 v1 .1"
  fam1_birth_months = 3 "FAM-1 v1 .3"
  fam1_file_day = 04-30 "FAM-1 v1 .2: filed by 30 April before the period"

version fam1_v2
  cite fam_1
  governs 2024-01..
  known 2023-08-10
  note "FAM-1 v2, in force 2024-01-01 until replaced, published 2023-08-10; governs months from 2024-01 (points 2–5 as v1)."
  fam1_age = 18 "FAM-1 v2 .1"
  fam1_amount = 650.00 "FAM-1 v2 .1"
  fam1_birth_months = 3 "FAM-1 v2 .3 (as v1)"
  fam1_file_day = 04-30 "FAM-1 v2 .2 (as v1): filed by 30 April before the period"
,11:GEN-1.tally,4072:part gen_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "GEN-1 · Business days and public holidays. holidays is the calendar next_business and prev_business read (L §4.2): one row per year, the fixed days of GEN-1 .2 plus that year's Spring Day from its notice (HOL-SPRING-<yyyy>)."
  note "A year's row sits in the version of its Spring Day notice, known on the notice's publication day: a dates value is one list, so the fixed days, settled since 2017-06-01 (2024-06-18 for 23 June), can't be known before the notice that completes the list (observation O:A-3). A year with no notice has no row (GEN-1 .3)."

source gen_1 "General Provisions Act, GEN-1 Business days and public holidays (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input holidays: calendar question "Which days of this year are public holidays (GEN-1 .2, and the Spring Day notice of GEN-1 .3)?"

