,11:GEN-5.tally,850:part gen_5
  tally 2
  law
  note "GEN-5 · Rounding. PIT, IGT and TT bases, taxes and advances to whole dukats, under 50 orts down, from 50 up (.1: round(x, 1, half-up)); VAT on an invoice to the ort half up, VAT due or carried in a return to whole dukats as .1 (.2); contributions, benefits, refunds and fees to the ort half up (.3); a rule's own rounding replaces these (.4); nothing else is rounded (.5)."
  note "No figure: the rounding units 1 and 0.01 are literals the literal rule allows (L §7.1); the households' defs call round at the step .5 names."

source gen_5 "General Provisions Act, GEN-5 Rounding (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version gen5_v1
  cite gen_5
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-06-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "GEN-5 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-06-01; governs every amount this law computes."
,11:GEN-6.tally,845:part gen_6
  tally 2
  law
  note "GEN-6 · Figures set by notice. Holds the Official Gazette as a source: every gazette figure is a row in its own version, known on the notice's publication day and governing the notice's in-force span (GEN-6 .1); a day no notice covers has no row, so what the law computes from it is a hole (GEN-6 .2, gap rule L §4.6)."
  note "Figures and tables only: the households' own defs apply them and point at these versions with v."

source gazette "Official Gazette of Lenia, notices of figures (tmp/cases/law/gazette.csv)"

source gen_6 "General Provisions Act, GEN-6 Figures set by notice (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version gen6_v1
  cite gen_6
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-06-01
  note "GEN-6 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-06-01; governs every figure the law leaves to a notice."
,11:IGT-1.tally,696:part igt_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "IGT-1 · What is taxed: what a person acquires by inheritance or by gift, the person or the asset being in Lenia (.1); the acquirer's groups I, II and III (.2), held as the index igt_group of IGT-3."
  note "No figure. A sum an insurer pays to a named beneficiary is not acquired by inheritance, so it is outside .1 (and exempt from PIT, PIT-14)."

source igt_1 "Inheritance and Gift Tax Act, IGT-1 What is taxed, and the groups (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

