  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-06-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "GEN-2 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-06-01; governs every deadline in this law."
,11:GEN-3.tally,934:part gen_3
  tally 2
  law
  note "GEN-3 · Periods and ages. A period of n months or years from a day ends on the same day number n months (years) on, or on that month's last day (.1): add_months and add_years (L §4.2) say the same. From a month's end, on the last day of the n-th month after it (.2). Within a period is on or before its last day (.3). Age n on the n-th anniversary of birth, 28 February for a birth on 29 February (.4; age() of L §4.2 takes 1 March, a difference household D doesn't reach). A month is a calendar month (.5)."
  note "No figure: the households' defs apply it through add_months, add_years and age."

source gen_3 "General Provisions Act, GEN-3 Periods and ages (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version gen3_v1
  cite gen_3
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-06-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "GEN-3 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-06-01; governs every period and age in this law."
,11:GEN-4.tally,2808:part gen_4
  tally 2
  law
  note "GEN-4 · Amounts in a foreign currency. An amount in florens is converted at the Central Bank's mid rate FX-FLR of the last business day before the event's day (.1), each amount alone, rounded to whole orts half up (.2); a bank's own rate is never used under the law (.3)."
  note "fx_mid holds the gazette's FX-FLR rows, each in its own version known on its publication day and governing that one day (gazette from = to); the households read it at prev_business(add_days(d, -1), holidays) through a def's at (L §4.3). A day with no row is a hole (GEN-6 .2)."

source gen_4 "General Provisions Act, GEN-4 Amounts in a foreign currency (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

