  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "PIT-10 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs tax years from 2018 and advances for months from January 2018."
  pit10_flat_rate[it] = 0.12 "PIT-10 v1 .4: IT services 12 %"
  pit10_flat_rate[services] = 0.085 "PIT-10 v1 .4: other services 8.5 %"
  pit10_flat_rate[asset_sale] = 0.10 "PIT-10 v1 .4: the sale of a business asset 10 %"
  pit10_profit_rate = 0.19 "PIT-10 v1 .1 (b): 19 % of profit"
,12:PIT-11.tally,1061:part pit_11
  tally 2
  law
  note "PIT-11 · Cars in a business. Under (a) and (b), a car used privately too counts 75 % of its running costs (.1); depreciation 20 % a year of the initial value (net price plus the VAT not deducted), 1/12 a month from the month after its entry in the asset register to the month of its sale, each month rounded to the ort half up (.2); its sale under (a) or (b) (.3); under (c) the net price is revenue at the asset-sale rate (.4)."

source pit_11 "Personal Income Tax Act, PIT-11 Cars in a business (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input pit11_depreciation: num question "What is a car's yearly depreciation rate (PIT-11 .2)?"

input pit11_running_share: num question "What share of a mixed-use car's running costs counts as costs (PIT-11 .1)?"

version pit11_v1
  cite pit_11
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "PIT-11 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs tax years from 2018."
  pit11_depreciation = 0.20 "PIT-11 v1 .2"
  pit11_running_share = 0.75 "PIT-11 v1 .1"
,12:PIT-12.tally,1452:part pit_12
  tally 2
  law
  note "PIT-12 · The sale of a dwelling. Income is the price less the sale's costs less the acquisition cost (price, transfer tax, notary) (.1); taxed only when sold before the end of the 5th year after the acquisition's year (.2); 19 % of the income less the exempt part, base and tax rounded, in the return for the sale's year (.3); the exempt part is the income times the part of the price spent on the seller's own housing within 3 years after the end of the sale's year, over the price (.4); money spent after the return is filed corrects it (.5)."

source pit_12 "Personal Income Tax Act, PIT-12 The sale of a dwelling (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input pit12_rate: num question "What is the rate on a dwelling's sale (PIT-12 .3)?"

input pit12_spend_years: int question "Within how many years after the end of the sale's year does spending on housing count (PIT-12 .4)?"

input pit12_taxed_years: int question "Until the end of which year after acquisition is a sale taxed (PIT-12 .2)?"

