  cite pit_4
  governs 2018-01-01..2021-12-31
  known 2017-09-01
  note "PIT-4 v1, in force 2018-01-01 – 2021-12-31, published 2017-09-01; governs advances on payments made 2018-01-01 – 2021-12-31."

version pit4_v2
  cite pit_4
  governs 2022-01-01..
  known 2021-11-15
  note "PIT-4 v2, in force 2022-01-01 until replaced, published 2021-11-15; governs advances on payments made from 2022-01-01 (points 1–3 as v1, without the health contribution)."

version pit4_v2_p4
  cite pit_4
  governs 2022-07-01..2022-12-31
  known 2021-11-15
  note "PIT-4 v2 point 4: for payments made 2022-07-01 – 2022-12-31, the lower of the advance under PIT-3 v2 and under PIT-3 v3."
  pit4_lower_wording = 2022-06-30 "PIT-4 v2 .4 names PIT-3 v2, whose wording was in force 2022-01-01 – 2022-06-30 (PIT-3 v2 in-force line)"
,11:PIT-5.tally,1127:part pit_5
  tally 2
  law
  note "PIT-5 · The yearly return. The year's base is the sum of the person's PIT-2 bases from every payer, rounded (.2); the tax is the PIT-3 tax of the version governing the year, less the child relief, (v1: less the year's health contributions up to 7.75 % of their bases), never below 0, rounded (.3); less the advances (.4). No figures of its own: the households' return defs point at these versions."

source pit_5 "Personal Income Tax Act, PIT-5 The yearly return (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input pit5_refund_days: int question "Within how many days of filing does the RO refund (PIT-5 .4)?"

