,11:SOC-7.tally,3102:part soc_7
  tally 2
  law
  note "SOC-7 · The survivor pension. v1 (months 2018-01 – 2025-06): a spouse aged 50 or over at the death is entitled to 85 % of the pension the deceased was entitled to on the day of the death, rounded, indexed as if it had started when the deceased's started (.1); paid from the month after the death if claimed within 12 months, otherwise from the month after the claim; the deceased's pension for the month of the death is due in full (.2); of two pensions one is paid, the elected one (.3)."
  note "v2 (months from 2025-07, published 2024-12-12): .1 and .2 as v1; the elected pension in full and a part of the other, 15 % for months July 2025 – December 2026 and 25 % from January 2027, rounded, both together never more than 3 times the MIN-PENSION in force for the month, the part cut to fit (.3); on a claim, one filed by 30 September 2025 effective from July 2025, a later one from the month after it; months before the decision paid as arrears with the first payment after it (.4)."

source soc_7 "Social Insurance Act, SOC-7 The survivor pension (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input soc7_cap_mult: int question "How many times MIN-PENSION may both pensions together come to (SOC-7 v2 .3)?"

input soc7_claim_by: date question "By what day must the claim be filed to take effect from the start of v2 (SOC-7 v2 .4)?"

input soc7_claim_months: int question "Within how many months of the death must the claim be filed to be paid from the month after the death (SOC-7 .2)?"

input soc7_death_month_full: bool question "Is the deceased's pension for the month of the death due in full (SOC-7 .2)?"

input soc7_min_age: int question "From what age at the death is the spouse entitled (SOC-7 .1)?"

input soc7_part: num question "What part of the second pension is paid for this month (SOC-7 v2 .3)?"

input soc7_rate: num question "What share of the deceased's pension is the survivor pension (SOC-7 .1)?"

input soc7_v2_from: date question "From what day does a timely claim take effect (SOC-7 v2 .4)?"

version soc7_v1
  cite soc_7
  governs 2018-01-01..2025-06-30
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "SOC-7 v1, in force 2018-01-01 – 2025-06-30, published 2017-09-01; governs months 2018-01 – 2025-06."
  soc7_claim_months = 12 "SOC-7 v1 .2"
  soc7_death_month_full = true "SOC-7 v1 .2"
  soc7_min_age = 50 "SOC-7 v1 .1"
  soc7_rate = 0.85 "SOC-7 v1 .1"

version soc7_v2
  cite soc_7
  governs 2025-07-01..
  known 2024-12-12
  enters 2025-07-01
  note "SOC-7 v2, in force 2025-07-01 until replaced, published 2024-12-12; governs months from 2025-07."
  soc7_cap_mult = 3 "SOC-7 v2 .3"
  soc7_claim_by = 2025-09-30 "SOC-7 v2 .4"
  soc7_claim_months = 12 "SOC-7 v2 .2 (as v1)"
  soc7_death_month_full = true "SOC-7 v2 .2 (as v1)"
  soc7_min_age = 50 "SOC-7 v2 .1 (as v1)"
  soc7_part = 0.15 governs 2025-07-01..2026-12-31 "SOC-7 v2 .3: 15 % for months July 2025 – December 2026"
  soc7_part = 0.25 governs 2027-01-01.. "SOC-7 v2 .3: 25 % for months from January 2027"
  soc7_rate = 0.85 "SOC-7 v2 .1 (as v1)"
  soc7_v2_from = 2025-07-01 "SOC-7 v2 .4"
,11:SOC-8.tally,1861:part soc_8
  tally 2
  law
  note "SOC-8 · Parental pay: 52 weeks from the birth (birth day is day 1, .1); 100 % of the base for 20 weeks and 70 % for 32, or 81.5 % for all 52 when elected within 21 days (.2); base the average monthly gross of the 12 months before the birth month less 13.45 %, rounded (.3); a day's pay is base × rate / 30, rounded; a month's pay is the period's days in the month × a day's pay (.4); paid by the 10th of the next month, taxed under PIT-4 with the SIO as payer, no contributions (.5)."

source soc_8 "Social Insurance Act, SOC-8 Parental pay (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input soc8_base_cut: num question "What share is taken off the average gross for the base (SOC-8 .3)?"

input soc8_elect_days: int question "Within how many days of the birth is the election made (SOC-8 .2)?"

input soc8_pay_by: int question "By which day of the next month is a month's pay paid (SOC-8 .5)?"

input soc8_rate_elected: num question "What rate applies throughout when elected (SOC-8 .2)?"

input soc8_rate_first: num question "What rate applies in the first weeks (SOC-8 .2)?"

input soc8_rate_rest: num question "What rate applies in the later weeks (SOC-8 .2)?"

input soc8_weeks: int question "For how many weeks is parental pay due (SOC-8 .1)?"

input soc8_weeks_first: int question "How many weeks does the first rate last (SOC-8 .2)?"

