  cc2_fee_short = 0.005 "CC-2 v1 .2"
,11:CIV-1.tally,688:part civ_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "CIV-1 · Property of spouses: community property from the marriage unless a contract sets separate property (.1); community is what either acquires during the marriage, earnings and the income of separate assets included (.2); separate is what a spouse owned before, acquires by inheritance or gift (unless given to both), or in exchange for separate assets (.3)."

source civ_1 "Civil and Family Code, CIV-1 Property of spouses (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version civ1_v1
  cite civ_1
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-03-01
  note "CIV-1 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-03-01; governs marriages from any date, from 2018-01-01."
,11:CIV-2.tally,668:part civ_2
  tally 2
  law
  note "CIV-2 · The end of community property: on a spouse's death, divorce or a marital contract, that day (.1); from that day each spouse, or the deceased's estate, holds half of every community asset and owes half of every community debt (.2)."
  note "No figure: the half is the literal 2 (L §7.1) in the households' defs."

source civ_2 "Civil and Family Code, CIV-2 The end of community property (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version civ2_v1
  cite civ_2
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-03-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "CIV-2 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-03-01; governs ends of community from 2018-01-01."
,11:CIV-3.tally,855:part civ_3
  tally 2
  law
  note "CIV-3 · Succession by law: with no will the spouse and the children inherit in equal shares, the spouse's never below 1/4, the children sharing the rest equally (.1); a child who died before is replaced by its own children in equal parts (.2); the heirs hold the estate in their shares from the death until the division, and bear its debts in them (.3)."

source civ_3 "Civil and Family Code, CIV-3 Succession by law (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input civ3_spouse_min: num question "What is the least share of the estate the spouse inherits by law (CIV-3 .1)?"

